    {
      "caption": "Misconception: plant cells lack mitochondria",
      "duration_ms": 12000,
      "id": "s7",
      "narration": "It is tempting to hand mitochondria to animal cells and chloroplasts to plant cells — but plant cells respire too, burning the sugar photosynthesis makes, day and night. So plant cells have mitochondria as well; only the chloroplast is plant-only.",
